AOP: Aspect Oriented Programming
- It is way to add a extra behavior to your code without touching the actual business logic.
- Spring AOP works by creating a proxy around your bean, when we call a method a call first goes to the proxy.
  The proxy decides an aspect should run after the method, before the method or only when exception happens then it continues and call the actual method
- Using AOP we can keep our code clean and all cross cutting concerns are handed in one place.